\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.14cm, y=0.7cm]
\draw[xstep=1, ystep=0.2, black!20, dotted] (0,0) grid (50,14);
\draw[xstep=10, ystep=1, black!20, thin] (0,0) grid (50,14);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(51,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,14.6);
\foreach \x in {0,10,20,30,40,50} \node[below] at (\x,0) {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {0,1,...,14} \node[left] at (0,\y) {$\y$};
\draw[very thick] (0,0)--(5.5,0)--(21,3)--(39,9)--(44.8,14);
\node at (33,6.4) {\textbf{A}};
\node at (25,-1.4) {Taxable income (thousands of dollars)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-8,7) {Tax payable (thousands of dollars)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

answer.worked:
Section A connects the point $(21, 3)$ and $(39, 9)$. Using the gradient formula $m = \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$:
$$\begin{aligned}
m &= \frac{9 - 3}{39 - 21} \\
&= \frac{6}{18} \\
&= \frac{1}{3}
\end{aligned}$$

