content.prompt:
At a World Cup rugby match, the stadium was filled to capacity for the entire game.
At the end of the game, people left the stadium at a constant rate.
The graph shows the number of people ($N$) in the stadium $t$ minutes after the end of the game.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.1cm, y=0.00003cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(56,0) node[below right] {$t$ (minutes)};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,78000) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (0,60000)--(30,0);
\fill (0,60000) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (30,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[left] at (0,60000) {$60\,000$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node[below] at (30,0) {$30$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The equation of the line is of the form $N = a - bt$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants.

answer.worked:
$$\begin{aligned}
N &= a - bt \\
bt &= a - N \\
t &= \frac{a - N}{b}
\end{aligned}$$

$$\begin{aligned}
\text{Number of people remaining} (N) &= 60000 - 10000 = 50000 \\
t &= \frac{60000 - 50000}{2000} \\
&= \frac{10000}{2000} \\
&= 5 \text{ minutes}
\end{aligned}$$

The new graph should follow the original line until $t = 15$ (where $N = 30000$)
then from that point, continue as a straight line with a shallower slope, intersecting the $t$-axis at some $t > 30$.
The diagram shows one possible continuation; any shallower straight continuation from this point meeting the $t$-axis beyond $t=30$ is admissible.
[tikz]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.1cm, y=0.00003cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(56,0) node[below right] {$t$ (minutes)};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,78000) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (0,60000)--(30,0);
\fill (0,60000) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (30,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[left] at (0,60000) {$60\,000$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node[below] at (30,0) {$30$};
\draw[blue, very thick] (15,30000)--(45,0);
\fill[blue] (15,30000) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

